FWIW, I use the partial menus. That yields a dialogue like

| What would you like to drop?    |
|          Coins                  |
| -  S [@] 448 gold pieces        |
|          Weapons                |
| -  a [@] a +1 elven dagger      |
| 21 j [@] 42 uncursed darts      |
|All k [@] 3 cursed crude daggers |

where [@] is the appropriate tile and the pipes on the side force me to
apologize to anyone reading with proportional fonts. ;~)

So clicking (or tapping on a PDA) the field to the left will bring up a
"Count" dialog box (letting me drop only half my darts). Clicking anywhere
to the right of that -- the inventory character, icon, or item name --
will toggle between all and none (represented by a single hyphen). On the
Zaurus, the text also turns green when picking up or dropping any
quantity, but ymmv.




